n flank institutional architecture is deepening independently of US bilateral engagement. The European strategic autonomy track continues on its own trajectory. But the week's balance of signals tilts toward increased exposure: the US relationship is less reliable than the prior assessment reflected, the informal channels operating within the Trump administration are more consequential and less predictable than the dual-track framework captured, and the domestic political battle over security leadership is now consuming bandwidth across all institutional actors simultaneously.",
